demos/cert-hygiene/.lab-logs/

# Recorded lab runs live in the bucket and the evidence release, not here; only their
# manifests are committed -- discovery runs included, the same as every other run. The
# current control run is the exception that must stay on disk, because the
# control-at-tree validity rule reads it from there, so it is ignored rather than
# deleted. (A handful of discovery runs were committed whole before this rule was
# corrected; those stay in history as an exception, not a pattern to repeat.)
/demos/cert-hygiene/runs/*/*/
